<title>USA: Xoma enters new licensing deals.</title>
<headline>Xoma enters new licensing deals.</headline>
<dateline>BERKELEY, Calif. 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Xoma Corp said Monday it entered licensing deals with Eli Lilly and Co and Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn for the use of its patented technology for pharmaceutical production.</p>
<p>The latest deals bring to 10 the number of companies that have licensed the Xoma technology. Xoma says its system reduces production costs, incrases product yields and improves process control in the manufacture of genetically-engineered pharmaceuticals.</p>
</text>
